/**
 * Where each game's files live on the guest — the single source of truth for the
 * customer Files tab's "Game files" control (components/customer/files/GameFilesBar.tsx).
 *
 * Plain, side-effect-free module: it is imported by a server page AND by the
 * "use client" file browser, so it must never import anything server-only.
 *
 * `gameFilesPath` is the folder a customer should LAND in to find the game's
 * server files, configs, mods/plugins folder and worlds/saves. It is a root-
 * absolute path in the file browser's virtual filesystem (which IS the guest's
 * real filesystem — the Files tab reads the guest as root over SFTP).
 *
 * HOW EACH ENTRY WAS DERIVED. Not guessed: from the `-v host:container` bind
 * mounts in each family's setupScript (prisma/catalog.ts, prisma/seed-wave*-games.ts;
 * later waves override earlier ones, e.g. unturned), the applier specs
 * (lib/game-applier-specs/*) and the mod installers (lib/mods/installers/*).
 * `source` records how far an entry has been checked:
 *   - "verified-live"     — `test -d` run against a real RUNNING customer guest
 *                           (2026-10-05, read-only, directory names only) for the
 *                           landing folder and every shortcut listed.
 *   - "from-setup-script" — derived from the code above; no running server of that
 *                           family was reachable/existing to confirm. The UI copes
 *                           either way: a missing folder falls back to the nearest
 *                           existing parent (nearestExistingParent below).
 * A "verified-live" entry with variant-specific shortcuts was verified on the
 * variant(s) named in `note`; the others stay derived from the installers.
 *
 * ADDING A GAME: add its family to GAME_FAMILIES (lib/games.ts) AND an entry here.
 * test/game-files-roots.test.ts fails the build of a family without one.
 *
 * Landing-folder rule: the host folder that holds what customers actually edit.
 * Where one bind mount holds everything, that mount. Where config and game install
 * are separate mounts (valheim, projectzomboid), the config side, with the install as
 * a shortcut. Where two sibling mounts are equally important and self-explanatory
 * (vrising, conan, sdtd...), their common parent, with each as a shortcut.
